# Citation metadata. At each GitHub release Zenodo adds the DOI and the release date.
# The pyDAC paper is in `references` (a ChemRxiv preprint for now).
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pyDAC in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "pyDAC: simulation of adsorption-based direct air capture processes"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Mattia
    family-names: Galanti
  - given-names: Ivo
    family-names: Roghair
  - given-names: Martin
    family-names: van Sint Annaland
license: MIT
version: 3.0.1
repository-code: "https://github.com/process-intensification-lab/pyDAC"
keywords:
  - direct air capture
  - adsorption
  - TVSA
  - cyclic adsorption
  - packed bed
  - process simulation
abstract: >-
  pyDAC simulates adsorption cycles composed from configurable steps (by default a
  steam-assisted temperature-vacuum swing adsorption, TVSA, cycle) for CO2 direct air capture
  in 1D and 2D packed beds: single step sequences, cycles to cyclic steady state with KPIs, and
  local NSGA-II optimization of the operating conditions.
references:
  - type: article
    status: preprint
    title: "pyDAC: Open-Source two-dimensional modeling of s-TVSA for direct air capture: experimental assessment and validity of one-dimensional approximations"
    authors:
      - given-names: Mattia
        family-names: Galanti
      - given-names: Ivo
        family-names: Roghair
      - given-names: Martin
        family-names: van Sint Annaland
    journal: ChemRxiv
    year: 2026
    doi: 10.26434/chemrxiv.15010382/v1
    url: "https://doi.org/10.26434/chemrxiv.15010382/v1"
